# Integer8 addition promotes overflow to int16

Adds 1 to the int8 maximum to verify the result promotes to int16 instead
of failing, then adds 1 again to verify chained arithmetic keeps using the
promoted representation. Both declarations keep the static int8 type while
the runtime values use the wider precision.

>>> source
const maximum: int8 = 127
const unit: int8 = 1

const overflow: int8 = maximum + unit
print(overflow)

const chained: int8 = overflow + unit
print(chained)

<<< stdout
128
129

<<< stderr
